### META
directory_path: install/_setup.sh/cli
description: DINSER CLI tools and modular command system
created: 2025-01-28
modified: 2025-01-28
status: active

### FILES
dinser | Main DINSER CLI (modular v2.0 per PART 6.5)
dinser.old | Previous non-modular version (backup)
setup.sh | CLI setup/installation script

### DIRECTORIES
commands/ | Modular command handlers

### CLI_ARCHITECTURE
Core commands (hardcoded in dinser):
- version, -v, --version
- help, -h, --help
- status
- setup (with --init, --from-beginning)
- webui (subcommands: up, down, status, logs, etc.)

Modular commands (auto-discovered from commands/):
- check (diagnostics per PART 6.3)
- test (test runner per PART 6.5.4)
- (additional commands can be added as .sh files)

### ADDING_COMMANDS
To add a new command:
1. Create commands/<n>.sh
2. Define cmd_<n>() function
3. Add # description: comment
4. dinser auto-discovers it

### DEPENDENCIES
setup.sh referenced by dinser for setup command
webui.sh (in parent) for webui command
commands/*.sh for modular commands

### NOTES
Per PART 6.5.1, dinser uses:
- Hardcoded core commands (stable, documented)
- Dynamic command discovery (extensible)
